<https://id.i2idl.org/definitions/learning-trajectories> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "ERIC scope note: The sequence of skills and knowledge students should learn as they move from one grade, age, or developmental stage to another. May also include instructional activities to support learning at each level." <https://id.i2idl.org/graphs/concepts/learning-trajectories/versions/1> .
<https://id.i2idl.org/definitions/learning-trajectories> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://glossarystudio.app/ns/Definition> <https://id.i2idl.org/graphs/concepts/learning-trajectories/versions/1> .
<https://id.i2idl.org/definitions/learning-trajectories> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#value> "Descriptions of how knowledge and skills may develop across successive stages, used to inform learning goals, instruction, and assessment." <https://id.i2idl.org/graphs/concepts/learning-trajectories/versions/1> .
